<title>SINGAPORE: First Kekwah crude lifting delayed two weeks-trade.</title>
<headline>First Kekwah crude lifting delayed two weeks-trade.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The lifting of the first cargo of Malaysia's new Bunga Kekwah crude will be delayed to the second half of August, instead of the initially planned first half of August, said an industry source.</p>
<p>The delay was due to minor glitches in the production start up of the field, the source said.</p>
<p>Malaysia's state-owned trading company Petco was expected to issue a tender within the next two weeks to sell the first Bunga Kekwah crude cargo.  </p>
<p>The consortium developing the field is made up of Petronas Carigali, with 46.06 percent, Petrovietnam Exploration and Production with 12.5 percent, Canada's International Petroleum Corp with 26.44 percent and Sands Petroleum AB with 15 percent.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65 870 3571)</p>
</text>
